Bound the generated fixed-size contig decode copy against the bytes received.

The xdrzcc generator emits a fixed opaque[N] contig copy out of the read
cursor's current iovec without first checking that N bytes remain.  Emit a
remaining-bytes guard immediately before that copy, using the same
compile-time N: the single-iovec contig wrapper is
chosen only when the whole message is one iovec (niov == 1, cur == last), so
xdr_read_cursor_remaining() returns exactly the bytes still present.  The
helper is the one added to xdr_builtin.c by 0001 and embedded into every
generated translation unit, so the emitted decoder can call it.

(git apply ignores this free-text preamble and starts at the diff --git line.)

diff --git a/src/xdrzcc.c b/src/xdrzcc.c
--- a/src/xdrzcc.c
+++ b/src/xdrzcc.c
@@ -345,6 +345,9 @@ emit_unmarshall_contig(
 
     if (type->opaque) {
         if (type->array) {
+            fprintf(output,
+                    "    if (unlikely((uint64_t) %s > xdr_read_cursor_remaining(cursor))) { return -1; }\n",
+                    type->array_size);
             fprintf(output,
                     "    memcpy(out->%s, (char *) xdr_iovec_data(cursor->cur) + cursor->iov_offset, %s);\n",
                     name, type->array_size);
